  "simplified": [
    "The approach and six suspended bays follow one azimuth. The roadway rises toward the central anchorage in broad grades.",
    "Each pentagonal suspender represents a pair of ropes. The cable bundles and steel bracing use enlarged sections for phone-scale visibility. Hanger stations are approximately 28 m apart.",
    "The two roadways and outer diagonals retain the double-deck outline. Lane markings, railings, lights, individual rivets and underwater caissons are omitted.",
    "The model stops at a grounded, open terminal bent on the San Francisco approach and the solid end anchorage on Yerba Buena Island. The W4 cable entry is scaled from the exterior elevation.",
    "West of transition pier W1, the main cables descend through and below the double deck into two grouped land-side housings. The outermost ends of the San Francisco anchorage are cropped."
  ],
